{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CfNp1RUqQ6i4bQM6d4DKG","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The project is set up and cross-compiles cleanly to a Windows PE64 executable.\n\n**What was done:**\n- `cargo init` scaffolded a new binary crate (`winapi-demo`).\n- Added `winapi = \"0.3.9\"` with a few common features (`winuser`, `libloaderapi`, `consoleapi`, `processthreadsapi`) to `Cargo.toml`. Cargo automatically pulled in `winapi-x86_64-pc-windows-gnu` as a transitive dependency — that's the crate holding the `.a` import libraries winapi needs for the GNU toolchain, so no manual wiring was needed there.\n- Added `.cargo/config.toml` setting the default build target to `x86_64-pc-windows-gnu` and pointing the linker at `x86_64-w64-mingw32-gcc` (already installed on this machine).\n- Wrote a minimal `src/main.rs` calling `MessageBoxA` via the winapi bindings, to exercise the toolchain end-to-end.\n- Verified with `cargo build`: it compiled and produced `target/x86_64-pc-windows-gnu/debug/winapi-demo.exe`, confirmed via `file` to be a valid PE32+ Windows executable.\n\nNext steps if you want: run `cargo build --release` for an optimized binary, or add more winapi feature flags as you bind additional APIs."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":270,"cache_read_input_tokens":21627,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":270},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9b4a8cff-c1ae-4317-8570-7d1f929b56b4","uuid":"7fc35082-3231-4287-affe-5326464dc40f","timestamp":"2026-09-24T19:24:24.796Z","request_id":"req_011CfNp1R2nmmqRdwujansEA"}
